  "details": "I'm proposing an enhancement to the camera follow mode for streamers. The current mode centers the avatar, which isn't ideal for stream aesthetics, especially when integrating chat overlays.\n\nFeature Request: \n\nAn option to adjust the avatar's position within the camera frame to follow the rule-of-thirds, offering positions to the left, right, or center. This could be implemented via:\n\nPrimary Option: \n\nIntegrate an X/Y position adjustment feature similar to the focus select, offering complete flexibility in positioning the avatar within the frame.\n\nAlternative Option: \n\nOffer simple preset positions (left, center, right) for those favoring ease over detailed customization, aligning with the classic rule of thirds or golden ratio composition.\n\nBenefits:\n\nAllows for more aesthetically pleasing stream compositions.\n\nImproves screen space utilization for overlays and other elements.\n\nThank you for considering this addition to support VRChat's content creator community.",
